{"abstract":[{"text":"Clears the local identity, super properties, and timed events via","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"MixpanelInstance.reset(completion:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and returns once that is done.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Init-time super properties are then re-applied."}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reset","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Everything still queued is sent first, and this waits for it: the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"SDK’s own "},{"code":"reset()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends one 50-record batch and deletes the rest.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Anything the network then fails to take is discarded, as the SDK does."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"While opted out this only forgets the adapter’s record of the user.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Opting out has already cleared the SDK’s identity and queue, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SDK’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"reset()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" would also erase the persisted opt-out — the user","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"would be tracked again from the next launch.","type":"text"}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/MixpanelAnalyticsService\/reset()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/mixpanelanalyticsservice\/reset()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"s